    "knowledge_point": "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function",
    "problem": "Calculate the period of the function $f(x)=-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{8x-\\pi }{4}).$",
    "worked_solution": "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that\n\n$$\nf(x)=-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{8x-\\pi }{4})=-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=2,$ and so the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$",
